      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242039",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/0f/0f95ea5e6fbadfb074704c04c44eabca4ce5ef61057f6eadf21088cff3f02102.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $AK^(\u2015)$, $BL^(\u2015)$, and $CM^(\u2015)$ are the medians of $\u25b3ABC$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The medians of $\u25b3ABC$ are concurrent.*\n\nSelect the correct options in the proof below.\n\nLet $G$ be the point of intersection of $AK^(\u2015)$ and $BL^(\u2015)$, and let $H$ be the point of intersection of $AK^(\u2015)$ and $CM^(\u2015)$.\n\nSince $AK^(\u2015)$ and $BL^(\u2015)$ are {{field-1}} of $\u25b3ABC$, by\n{{field-2}},\nwe have that {{field-3}} splits $AK^(\u2015)$ in the ratio {{field-4}}, starting from the point {{field-5}}."
    },
